  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human-centred recovery and Decent Work agenda reflected in the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Frameworks and Decent Work Country Programmes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO is supporting the just transition process that aims to provide decent job opportunities and social justice within the framework of challenges related to environmental sustainability . It also emphasizes the need to protect workers&#x2019; rights and ensure their effective participation in the transition to a green economy . Just transition policies seek to reduce the negative impacts of economic and environmental transitions on workers and communities, especially those in carbon-dependent industries or regions . Within this context, ILO believes that green jobs can drive economic growth, create decent and sustainable job opportunities, and contribute to reducing poverty , as this sector is expected to create 100 million jobs by 2030. 
At the regional level, the GCC countries affirm their keenness to transition to a more sustainable economy and focus on renewable energy, biodiversity, and environmental preservation by adopting national plans for sustainable development and the green economy, and are working to enhance investment in green sectors, promote innovation, and develop environmental technology .
ILO will be supporting the GCC countries in formulating policies and programs aimed at enhancing and raising the skills of the workforce in the green economy .</narrative>
  </description>
